# MCSP DMA Transfer Projection 0.34

Status: Constructive non-CPU realization model
Qualification: Under Conditional Experiment

## Purpose

Test whether MCSP pre-settlement and preservation can cross from processor-instruction realizations into a DMA-style transfer realization without making CPU instructions, registers, opcodes, or instruction count part of the semantic invariant.

This checkpoint models a DMA realization contract. It does not claim execution by a physical DMA controller.

## Pre-settled transfer invariant

For the declared fixture, the material invariant is:

- source role;
- destination role;
- transfer extent;
- material payload distinctions;
- completion requirement;
- failure state;
- forbidden-effect condition;
- provenance/dependency token when declared material.

The following remain realization-defined:

- DMA controller identity;
- descriptor binary format;
- bus address representation;
- queue/ring organization;
- cache-coherency mechanism;
- interrupt/polling completion mechanism;
- physical path;
- burst width;
- scheduling;
- implementation timing.

## Bootstrap descriptor projection

The 0.34 structural projection is:

    source_token
    destination_token
    extent
    payload_token
    provenance_token
    completion
    failure
    forbidden_effect

This tuple is qualification scaffolding, not the MCSP kernel and not a universal DMA descriptor format.

## Preservation

A DMA-style realization satisfies the declared fixture only when:

1. source and destination roles remain applicable;
2. extent is preserved;
3. material payload distinctions are preserved;
4. required provenance/dependency is preserved;
5. completion satisfies the pre-settlement;
6. failure is not silently converted into success;
7. forbidden effects are absent.

Same final payload with wrong material provenance MUST fail when provenance is part of the pre-settlement.

## Hardware boundary

CPU execution of a validator can test the descriptor/projection contract.

That is not evidence that a physical DMA controller performed the transfer.

Qualification levels are therefore separated:

- DMA semantic projection;
- DMA descriptor/validator implementation;
- emulated/simulated DMA execution;
- physical DMA controller execution.

Only the applicable achieved level may be claimed.

Kernel remains DETERMINATE CONDITION.
